.TH SNAKED 1 snake
.SH NAME
snaked \- the snake game playing itself on the X desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snaked
.RB [ \-b
.IR RRGGBB ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR PX ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR RRGGBB ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR RRGGBB ]
.RB [ \-F
.IR RRGGBB ]
.RB [ \-S
.IR RRGGBB ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR MS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snaked
plays snake with the autopilot of
.BR snake (1)
on the whole screen, for ever: it goes at the food in a staircase,
never hits anything, fills the screen, and starts again. On the
desktop and the lock screen the snake is in clear colours; behind the
text of a terminal it is very faint, just lighter than the background.
.PP
It paints the desktop (the root window), and at every step puts the
board in the root window's
.B _SNAKE
property. Programs that read it draw the snake in their own empty
background, so that it seems to run behind them: the patched
.BR st (1)
behind the text of every terminal, wherever a cell's background is
the background colour (in vim and btop too), and the patched
.BR slock (1)
on the lock screen. Other programs cover it, as they would cover a
wallpaper. There is no compositor and no transparency.
.PP
Only one
.B snaked
runs on a display. It stops on SIGTERM or SIGINT
.RB ( "pkill snaked" ),
takes the snake off the screen and removes the property.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-b " RRGGBB"
background (default 1c1c1c, Habamax's)
.TP
.BI \-c " PX"
size of a cell in pixels (default 16)
.TP
.BI \-s " RRGGBB"
snake behind text, faint (default 242424)
.TP
.BI \-f " RRGGBB"
food behind text, a smaller square, faint (default 2b2620)
.TP
.BI \-S " RRGGBB"
snake on the desktop and the lock screen (default 87af87, Habamax
green)
.TP
.BI \-F " RRGGBB"
food on the desktop and the lock screen (default d787d7, Habamax
magenta)
.TP
.BI \-t " MS"
milliseconds per step (default 200)
.SH THE PROPERTY
.B _SNAKE
is a STRING: the line
.IP
.B snake2
.I SEQ CELL X Y W H SNAKE FOOD CSNAKE CFOOD
.PP
(the step count, a cell's size in pixels, the board's top left corner
on the screen, the board in cells, the faint colours and the clear
ones as RRGGBB), a
newline, then W times H bytes, row by row:
.B 0
empty,
.B 1
snake,
.B 2
food.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snake (1)
